        "original_id": "e6472022-7410-5e0b-a1ae-a99c93d1694b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Mōkōlea Rock, Kailua Bay, Oʻahu, Hawaiʻi, Mokapu Peninsula, windward Oʻahu, Honolulu\n- Organizations: Marine Corps Base Hawaii, U.S. Marine Corps\n- Names: Birdshit Island, Birdshit, Bird\n\nFacts:\n- Mōkōlea Rock is an islet in Kailua Bay on the windward coast of Oʻahu in Hawaiʻi.\n- Mōkōlea Rock is located east of Marine Corps Base Hawaii.\n- Local residents commonly call Mōkōlea Rock “Birdshit Island,” “Birdshit,” or “Bird” because its black lava rock surface is heavily coated with bird droppings.\n- Marine Corps Base Hawaii was formerly named Marine Corps Air Station Kaneohe Bay and was originally Naval Air Station Kaneohe Bay.\n- Marine Corps Base Hawaii is a U.S. Marine Corps facility and air station on the Mokapu Peninsula of windward Oʻahu in the City and County of Honolulu.",
